{# ============================================================================
   PATTERNS — the cycles this area fills a station from.

   PORTED FROM designs/…/modules/roster/configure-patterns.html, which is
   variants-pattern-editor option C.

   THE RULINGS THIS PAGE IS, in the owner's words: "users should be the ones
   defining the fill patterns, not the system forcing the user", and "the
   name should not be written by user but rather generated from the config
   the user chooses." So the product ships NO patterns, a cycle is said as a
   sentence out of this area's own shifts plus off, and there is no name
   field anywhere — the name is derived from the cycle, live in the editor
   and again on the server, by one function.

   ONE OBJECT AT AREA LEVEL, applied to stations from the Week sheet's fill
   row and not from here. Editing changes FUTURE FILLS ONLY: no day already
   planned moves, at any station running it, and a day somebody edited by
   hand is never touched. That is what makes one shared object safe.

   COVERAGE MANIFEST — every element of the drawn page.

   | element                          | type    | source                     | interaction            | status |
   |----------------------------------|---------|----------------------------|------------------------|--------|
   | h2.zone + p.pgsub (Week link)    | chrome  | static                     | link to the sheet      | done   |
   | header cta "New pattern"         | control | —                          | opens a blank editor   | done   |
   | editor .c (full width)           | state   | the chosen pattern, or new | —                      | done   |
   | .pfld label + .pdname            | data    | derived on every read      | none — read-only       | done   |
   | .pfld .len "N days long"         | data    | the cycle                  | none                   | done   |
   | .psbl one part: lead/n/shift     | control | the cycle, as runs         | edits the sentence     | done   |
   | .psbl a.x remove a part          | control | —                          | removes it             | done   |
   | "+ then…" + .psbhint             | control | —                          | adds a part            | done   |
   | .ppreview k / .pstrip / t        | data    | drawn from the same parts  | none                   | done   |
   | .pwhere info + where it runs     | data    | the stations running it    | none                   | done   |
   | Delete / Cancel / Save           | control | —                          | three writes, or none  | done   |
   | .pregc card per pattern          | data    | the register               | Edit opens it          | done   |
   | .pstrip on a card, +N overflow   | data    | the cycle                  | none                   | done   |
   | .at "running at N — names"       | data    | the stations running it    | none                   | done   |
   | .c.pnew                          | control | —                          | opens a blank editor   | done   |
   | empty register                   | state   | a fresh area fills by hand | none                   | done   |
   ========================================================================== #}
{% extends '@UhifadhiRoster/configure/_frame.html.twig' %}

{# WHETHER THIS PERSON MAY CHANGE HOW THE AREA FILLS A STATION — the pair
   both writes on this page carry. The page itself opens on the ground,
   so a reader sees the cycles with every control disabled. #}
{% set mayManage = door('roster.configure', area) %}

{% set here = path(constant('Uhifadhi\\Roster\\Controller\\RosterPatternsController::ROUTE'), {uuid: area.uuid}) %}
{% set blank = here ~ '?' ~ constant('Uhifadhi\\Roster\\Controller\\RosterPatternsController::NEW_QUERY') %}

{# HOW MANY DAYS A STRIP DRAWS BEFORE IT SAYS "+N". A card is BOUNDED: a
   twenty-eight day cycle must not make one card twice the height of the one
   beside it. #}
{% set strip_days = 14 %}

{# THE PAGE HEADER'S ONE ACCENT ACTION, beside the frame's Configure marker.
   Creating a pattern is a PAGE-LEVEL act (ruled 20 sep), so it is here and
   not a footer button and not a card header's door. #}
{# THE DESIGN'S OWN SUBLINE, as a fragment. #}
{% block shell_page_subtitle %}The cycles this area fills a station from &middot; a name is derived, never typed{% endblock %}

{% block shell_page_actions %}
    {% if mayManage %}<a class="cta" href="{{ blank }}">{{ ux_icon('shell:plus') }} New pattern</a>{% endif %}
{% endblock %}

{% block roster_section %}
<h2 class="zone" id="patterns">Patterns</h2>
{# TWO FRAGMENTS, no more. The derivation and the cycle are already said in
   the page subline above; what is left for the section to add is the one
   door — the sheet's fill row is where a pattern is applied, and this page
   offers no station picker at all — and what an edit reaches. #}
<p class="pgsub">Applied from the <a href="{{ path(constant('Uhifadhi\\Roster\\Controller\\RosterController::WEEK_ROUTE'), {uuid: area.uuid}) }}">Week sheet</a>&rsquo;s fill row &middot; editing reaches future fills only</p>

<div class="grid g2">

    {# ---- THE EDITOR ---------------------------------------------------
       A STATE OF THIS PAGE and not an address of its own: a cycle is said
       and then saved, and sending somebody to a second screen to do the
       first half would be two pages for one act. #}
    {% if open is not null or declaring %}
        {% set cycle = open is null ? [] : open.days %}
        <div class="c" style="grid-column:1/-1">
            <span class="tab">Pattern<span class="src">&middot; open</span></span>
            <form method="post" class="ptool" data-controller="roster--pattern-editor"
                  data-action="input->roster--pattern-editor#render change->roster--pattern-editor#render"
                  action="{{ path(constant('Uhifadhi\\Roster\\Controller\\RosterPatternsController::SAVE_ROUTE'), {uuid: area.uuid}) }}">
                <input type="hidden" name="_token" value="{{ csrfToken }}">
                {% if open is not null %}<input type="hidden" name="{{ constant('Uhifadhi\\Roster\\Controller\\RosterPatternsController::OPEN_QUERY') }}" value="{{ open.uuid }}">{% endif %}
                {# THE CYCLE GOES AS ONE FIELD, because it is validated as one
                   object: a ring applied half-way is a ring that plans a
                   month nobody asked for. The controller keeps it in step
                   with the sentence above it. #}
                <input type="hidden" name="{{ constant('Uhifadhi\\Roster\\Controller\\RosterPatternsController::CYCLE_FIELD') }}" value="[]" data-roster-cycle>

                <div class="pfld">
                    <label>Its name</label>
                    {# READ-ONLY BY RULE, so it must not look like something
                       you can type into: it is the TITLE of the thing. #}
                    <span class="pdname {{ open is null ? 'empty' : '' }}" data-roster-name>{{ open is null ? 'Build the cycle and the name writes itself' : open.name }}</span>
                    <span class="len" data-roster-length>{% if open is null %}nothing in the cycle yet{% else %}<b>{{ open.length }} day{{ open.length == 1 ? '' : 's' }} long</b>{% endif %}</span>
                </div>

                <div class="psb">
                    {% for part in runs %}
                        <div class="psbl" data-roster-part>
                            <span class="lead">{{ loop.first ? '' : 'then' }}</span>
                            <input class="psbn" value="{{ part.days }}" aria-label="How many days" data-roster-days>
                            {# THE WORD BETWEEN THE NUMBER AND THE SHIFT, kept
                               in step by the controller. The drawing writes
                               "1 day <shift>" and "2 days of <shift>"; the
                               derived name says "1 day of night", and one
                               wording is used here so the sentence and the
                               name above it read the same. #}
                            <span data-roster-unit>{{ part.days == 1 ? 'day' : 'days' }} of</span>
                            <select class="psbs" aria-label="Which shift" data-roster-shift>
                                {% for shift in shifts %}
                                    <option value="{{ shift.key }}" data-cat="{{ shift.colour }}" {{ shift.key == part.key ? 'selected' : '' }}>{{ shift.label }}</option>
                                {% endfor %}
                                <option value="off" {{ part.key == 'off' ? 'selected' : '' }}>off</option>
                            </select>
                            {% if not loop.first %}<button type="button" class="x" title="Remove this part" data-action="roster--pattern-editor#drop">&times;</button>{% endif %}
                        </div>
                    {% endfor %}
                    <div class="psbl">
                        <span class="lead"></span>
                        <button type="button" class="btn sm" data-action="roster--pattern-editor#add">+ then&hellip;</button>
                        <span class="psbhint">and round again from the start</span>
                    </div>
                </div>

                {# THE STRIP IS THE CYCLE, drawn from the same parts the
                   sentence names rather than written out beside them — so
                   the two cannot disagree, and neither needs a round trip. #}
                <div class="ppreview">
                    <span class="k">the cycle</span>
                    <span class="pstrip lg" data-roster-strip></span>
                    <span class="t">repeats for as long as a station runs it, then round again</span>
                </div>

                <div class="pwhere">
                    {{ ux_icon('shell:info') }}
                    <span>
                        {%- if open is null or open.stations is empty -%}
                            <b>No station is filled from this yet.</b> You apply it from the Week sheet&rsquo;s fill row, and it fills future days only.
                        {%- else -%}
                            <b>Running at {{ open.stations|join(', ') }}.</b> Saving a change here changes <b>future fills only</b> &mdash; no day already planned moves, and no day anybody edited by hand is ever touched.
                        {%- endif -%}
                    </span>
                </div>

                <div class="staddrow">
                    {% if open is not null %}
                        <button type="submit" class="btn sm dg" title="Delete this pattern"
                                formaction="{{ path(constant('Uhifadhi\\Roster\\Controller\\RosterPatternsController::DELETE_ROUTE'), {uuid: area.uuid, pattern: open.uuid}) }}">Delete this pattern</button>
                    {% endif %}
                    <span class="sp"></span>
                    <a class="btn sm" href="{{ here }}">Cancel</a>
                    <button type="submit" class="cta">Save this pattern</button>
                </div>
            </form>
        </div>
    {% endif %}

    {# ---- THE REGISTER --------------------------------------------------
       One card per pattern. The card's title IS the derived name, so it
       carries no .tab beyond the kind. #}
    {% for card in cards %}
        {% if open is null or card.uuid != open.uuid %}
            <div class="c">
                <span class="tab">Pattern</span>
                <div class="pregc">
                    <span class="nm">{{ card.name }}</span>
                    <span class="mt">{{ card.length }} day{{ card.length == 1 ? '' : 's' }} long &middot; the name is derived from the cycle</span>
                    <span class="pstrip">
                        {% for day in card.days|slice(0, strip_days) %}
                            <i class="pd {{ day.colour is null ? 'o' : '' }}" {% if day.colour is not null %}data-cat="{{ day.colour }}"{% endif %} title="{{ day.key }}"></i>
                        {% endfor %}
                        {% if card.length > strip_days %}<em class="pmore">+{{ card.length - strip_days }}</em>{% endif %}
                    </span>
                    <span class="at">
                        {%- if card.stations is empty -%}
                            no station is filled from it
                        {%- else -%}
                            running at <b>{{ card.stations|length }}</b> station{{ card.stations|length == 1 ? '' : 's' }} &mdash; {{ card.stations|join(', ') }}
                        {%- endif -%}
                    </span>
                    <span class="acts">
                        <span class="sp"></span>
                        <a class="btn sm" href="{{ here }}?{{ constant('Uhifadhi\\Roster\\Controller\\RosterPatternsController::OPEN_QUERY') }}={{ card.uuid }}">Edit</a>
                    </span>
                </div>
            </div>
        {% endif %}
    {% endfor %}

    {% if mayManage %}
        <div class="c pnew">
            <b>New pattern</b>Say a cycle and it gets a name. Nothing has to be filled in first.
            <a class="cta" href="{{ blank }}">+ New pattern</a>
        </div>
    {% elseif cards is empty %}
        <div class="c" style="grid-column:1/-1">
            <span class="tab">Patterns</span>
            <div class="pempty"><b>This area fills by hand</b>No cycle has been said yet, and the product ships none &mdash; a pattern is this area&rsquo;s own.</div>
        </div>
    {% endif %}
</div>
{% endblock %}
